  "lawGrade": "MAPPED",
  "lawGradeScale": "v4 law grading scale (native canon scale, strongest first): DERIVED, LOCKED, MAPPED, PARTIAL, SPLIT, OPEN, DEFINITIONAL. Mapping to C0-C6 unruled - tracked as OI-0011.",
  "statementTechnical": "Newton's Second Law F = dp/dt and Third Law F_12 = -F_21. Momentum conservation: internal forces sum to zero, so total momentum change requires an external force - redirection of a closed system requires external input. Amended (AM-2) from the retired Einstein-Meaning framing; E = mc^2 retained: mass and energy are the same thing measured differently. The mapping: mass/inertia is what resists change; meaning is what gives weight to existence; a life cannot be redirected from inside a closed system - the external force is read as grace. Action-reaction: every moral action produces counter-pressure.",
  "statementPlain": "You cannot redirect yourself. That is not a therapy insight - it is momentum conservation. Internal forces sum to zero; only an external force changes the total. The proposed reading: a closed life stays on its trajectory until something from outside acts on it, and the framework names that something grace. The mechanics are established; the meaning mapping is proposed, not proven - it remains open whether the parallel is structural or cosmetic. Its own kill condition says exactly how it would die.",
  "mathematicalForm": "F = dp/dt; F_12 = -F_21; sum(internal forces) = 0 => external force required for total momentum change; E = mc^2 retained",
  "mathFormNormal": "F = dp/dt; F_12 = -F_21; sum(internal forces) = 0 => external force required for total momentum change; E = mc^2 retained",
